00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: Add trending-metric verification step to TN bookend tasks for count-based acceptance criteria\\nDate: 2026-05-29\\nGoal: Add optional `trending_metric` sub-object to `AcceptanceCriterion`; extend T0 to capture integer counts; extend TN to assert count matches `target` and moved monotonically in `monotonic_direction`.\\nConditions:\\n1. `AcceptanceCriterion` model exists at `models.py:365-390` with no `trending_metric` field | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Read models.py:365-390 \u2014 class confirmed, no trending_metric field, grep returned 0 results\\n2. `BookendVerification` model exists at `models.py:421-449` with `stdout_diff_summary` but no `metric_history` field | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Read models.py:421-449 \u2014 fields confirmed: criterion_id, check_command, t0_exit_code, tn_exit_code, status, stdout_diff_summary only\\n3. `BookendResult` model exists at `models.py:393-418` capturing exit_code, stdout, stderr, timestamp, duration_seconds | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Read models.py:393-418 \u2014 fields confirmed as described\\n4. Shell command emitting a single integer is the external interface; uses existing Bash pattern in both agents | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Read t0-baseline-capture.md and tn-verification-gate.md \u2014 Bash pattern confirmed for command execution\\n5. `AcceptanceCriterion` uses `AliasChoices` throughout \u2014 new field must follow same pattern | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Grep AliasChoices in models.py \u2014 lines 375, 379, 383, 388 confirm consistent AliasChoices pattern on all AcceptanceCriterion fields\\n6. Backward-compatibility contract: field is optional with None default \u2192 existing criteria unaffected | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Read models.py:365-390 \u2014 all optional fields in AcceptanceCriterion and sibling models use Field(default=...) with None defaults. Pattern is established and unambiguous.\\n7. `BookendVerification` model representation for `metric_history` | Snapshot: MISSING \u2192 Final: PLANNER_DECISION | Citation: Two viable options documented in Design Intent Alignment section: (a) optional field on BookendVerification; (b) new TrendingMetricResult model. Both preserve backward compat. Decision deferred to planner with documented trade-offs \u2014 does not block grooming.\\n8. `t0-baseline-capture.md` agent procedure is compatible with branch-per-criterion extension | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Read t0-baseline-capture.md \u2014 Step 2 per-criterion loop at lines 44-57 confirmed. Branch addition is straightforward.\\n9. `tn-verification-gate.md` agent procedure is compatible with branch-per-criterion extension | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Read tn-verification-gate.md \u2014 Step 2 per-criterion loop at lines 57-63 confirmed. Branch addition is straightforward.\\n10. Research origin claim: `composio-codebase-migrate.md` lines 78-82 contains the verification loop pattern | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Read research/skill-generation-tools/composio-codebase-migrate.md lines 70-90 \u2014 section Verification Loop After Each Merge at lines 77-82 confirmed.\\nChanges from snapshot:\\n- Condition 6: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (resolved by reading models.py \u2014 Optional[X] = Field(default=None) is the established pattern throughout the file)\\n- Condition 7: MISSING \u2192 PLANNER_DECISION (not an information gap; two viable design options documented)\\n- Condition 8: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (resolved by reading t0-baseline-capture.md agent procedure)\\n- Condition 9: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (resolved by reading tn-verification-gate.md agent procedure)\\n- Condition 10: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (resolved by reading composio-codebase-migrate.md)\\nDecision: APPROVED\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **add trending-metric verification step to tn bookend tasks for count-based acceptance criteria** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/skill-generation-tools/composio-codebase-migrate.md \u2014 pattern: Verification Loop After Each Merge (rg 'pattern' | wc -l should trend to 0)\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-10\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-18)\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n**Verdict: APPROVED-WITH-GAPS**\\\\n\\\\n| Input | Status | Notes |\\\\n|---|---|---|\\\\n| Functional intent | PRESENT | Add optional `trending_metric` sub-object to `AcceptanceCriterion`; extend T0 to capture integer counts; extend TN to assert count matches `target` and moved monotonically in `monotonic_direction` |\\\\n| Scope boundaries | PRESENT | Bounded to: `AcceptanceCriterion` class at `models.py:365-390` (confirmed via Read - no `trending_metric` field exists), `BookendResult` at `models.py:393-418`, `BookendVerification` at `models.py:421-449`, `t0-baseline-capture.md`, `tn-verification-gate.md`, `tests_sam/test_models.py`, `TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` |\\\\n| External interfaces | PRESENT | Shell command emitting a single integer via stdout; uses existing `check_command` / Bash pattern already in both agents |\\\\n| Constraints | PARTIAL | Backward-compat is DERIVABLE (field is optional -> existing entries unaffected) but not yet explicit in model docstring or agent procedures |\\\\n| Existing system context | PRESENT | `AcceptanceCriterion` model verified at `models.py:365-390`; current fields: `criterion_id`, `description`, `check_command`, `expected_baseline`, `expected_final`; no `trending_metric` field exists; `BookendVerification` at `models.py:421-449` carries only `stdout_diff_summary` for diff content |\\\\n| Verification expectations | PRESENT | Measurable signal defined: `AcceptanceCriterion.model_fields` contains `trending_metric`; TN JSON output includes `metric_history`, `monotonic_violated`, `target_met` |\\\\n\\\\n**Gap (DERIVABLE)**: Backward-compatibility contract is implicit. Must be made explicit in `AcceptanceCriterion` docstring and both agent procedures.\\\\n\\\\n**Gap (MISSING)**: `BookendVerification` has no field for `metric_history`. Implementation must add it as an optional field on `BookendVerification` or create a separate `TrendingMetricResult` model. Item does not prescribe the choice - this is a planner decision.\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\nN/A for feature items.\\n\\nThis item is a schema extension request, not a bug. There is no defect to reproduce. The gap is observable by running:\\n\\n```bash\\nuv run python -c \\\"from sam_schema.core.models import AcceptanceCriterion; print('trending_metric' in AcceptanceCriterion.model_fields)\\\"\\n```\\n\\nExpected output: `False` (confirms gap exists pre-implementation).\\nAfter implementation, the same command should output `True`.\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n6/10 - Addresses a real gap in multi-file migration workflows (Composio pattern, jest to vitest migrations, import renaming). Unblocks encoding count-to-zero ACs as a single observable metric rather than per-file task lists. P2 is appropriate: high value for specific migration workloads, low urgency for the majority of feature implementations where binary pass/fail suffices.\\n\\nEffort: Medium \u2014 3 files to modify (`models.py`, `t0-baseline-capture.md`, `tn-verification-gate.md`), 1 file to update (`TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md`), 1 test class to extend (`test_models.py`). No new external dependencies. Schema addition is additive and backward-compatible. TN logic change is a conditional branch on an existing per-criterion loop.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: Multi-file migration plans that need a single observable \\\"count must reach 0\\\" AC \u2014 currently cannot express this without enumerating every file as a separate AC\\n- Bottleneck: Plan authors working on codemod or import-rename tasks must encode AC-as-task-list instead of AC-as-outcome, defeating the purpose of structured acceptance criteria\\n- Blast radius: `sam_schema/core/models.py`, `agents/t0-baseline-capture.md`, `agents/tn-verification-gate.md`, `tests_sam/test_models.py`, `docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md`\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Enables \\\"count of X must be 0\\\" as a single, machine-checkable acceptance criterion for migration tasks\\n- Eliminates the anti-pattern of encoding task-lists inside AC fields for multi-file changes\\n- T0 baseline automatically captures the initial count; TN asserts both target reached and monotonic progress\\n- Compatible with the codemod-runner skill (#2241) where per-batch verification trend commands are a core pattern\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen a plan's `acceptance-criteria-structured` entry includes a `trending_metric` sub-object, T0 runs the `command` and records the output integer alongside the normal exit-code result. TN re-runs the command, reads the T0 value, and asserts: (1) current value equals `target`, (2) direction of change from T0 to Tn matches `monotonic_direction`. When `trending_metric` is absent on a criterion, the existing binary exit-code comparison runs unchanged.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nThe target observable state:\\n\\n- `uv run python -c \\\"from sam_schema.core.models import AcceptanceCriterion; print('trending_metric' in AcceptanceCriterion.model_fields)\\\"` outputs `True`\\n- A YAML plan with a `trending_metric` entry round-trips through `AcceptanceCriterion.model_validate()` without error\\n- T0 baseline YAML for a plan with a `trending_metric` AC contains the integer output of the `command` alongside the normal `exit-code` and `stdout` fields\\n- TN verification JSON output for a criterion with `trending_metric` includes `metric_history: {t0_value: N, tn_value: M}`, `monotonic_violated: false|true`, and `target_met: true|false`\\n- Existing `AcceptanceCriterion` entries that omit `trending_metric` produce no change in T0/TN behavior\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `AcceptanceCriterion.model_fields` contains `trending_metric` as an optional field (default `None`)\\n2. `AcceptanceCriterion.model_validate({'criterion-id': 'AC-1', 'check-command': 'rg jest | wc -l', 'trending_metric': {'command': 'rg jest | wc -l', 'target': 0, 'monotonic_direction': 'decreasing'}})` succeeds without error\\n3. `AcceptanceCriterion.model_validate({'criterion-id': 'AC-1', 'check-command': 'pytest'})` succeeds unchanged (backward compat)\\n4. T0 baseline YAML for a plan containing a `trending_metric` AC includes a `metric_value` integer field in the result entry for that criterion\\n5. TN verification output for the same criterion includes `metric_history` dict with `t0_value` and `tn_value` keys, `monotonic_violated` bool, and `target_met` bool\\n6. TN sets `verdict: FAIL` when `target_met: false` or `monotonic_violated: true` for any criterion with `trending_metric`\\n7. `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_models.py -k trending_metric` exits 0 with at least 4 test cases: construction with trending_metric, construction without (backward compat), model_dump round-trip, validation error on invalid monotonic_direction\\n8. `TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` documents `trending_metric` sub-fields under the `acceptance-criteria-structured` section\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Source model | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py:365\u2013390` (`AcceptanceCriterion`) |\\n| Source model | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py:393\u2013449` (`BookendResult`, `BookendVerification`) |\\n| Agent | `plugins/development-harness/agents/t0-baseline-capture.md` |\\n| Agent | `plugins/development-harness/agents/tn-verification-gate.md` |\\n| Test file | `plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_models.py` (existing `TestAcceptanceCriterionModel` at line 765) |\\n| Research origin | `research/skill-generation-tools/composio-codebase-migrate.md` lines 78\u201382 |\\n| Improvement notes | `research/insights/2026-05-10-composio-codebase-migrate-improvements.md` lines 56\u201375 |\\n| Related feature | Backlog #2241 \u2014 codemod-runner skill |\\n| Skill reference | `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md:278\u2013304` (Bookend Task Ordering) |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 `AcceptanceCriterion` model is self-contained\\n- Blocks: Backlog #2241 (codemod-runner skill) benefits from this but does not strictly require it\\n- Related: Backlog #2240 (per-wave PR mode in work-milestone) \u2014 orthogonal, no dependency\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\nNone blocking. The single DERIVABLE gap (backward-compat contract) is resolved by making the field optional with `None` default and documenting the invariant.\\n\\nImplementation decision for planner: whether `metric_history` lives on `BookendVerification` (optional field) or a new `TrendingMetricResult` model. Both approaches preserve backward compat.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nMedium \u2014 3 files to modify (`models.py`, `t0-baseline-capture.md`, `tn-verification-gate.md`), 1 file to update (`TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md`), 1 test class to extend (`test_models.py`). No new external dependencies. Schema addition is additive and backward-compatible. TN logic change is a conditional branch on an existing per-criterion loop.\\n\\n**Implementation note**: `AcceptanceCriterion` uses `AliasChoices` throughout. The new field must follow the same alias pattern (`validation_alias=AliasChoices('trending-metric', 'trending_metric')`, `serialization_alias='trending-metric'`) for consistency with the rest of the model.\\n\\n### Agent Instructions (instruct AI to use current interface)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/t0-baseline-capture.md` \u2014 Procedure must be updated (see Code \u2014 Producers above).\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/tn-verification-gate.md` \u2014 Procedure must be updated (see Code \u2014 Producers above).\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Consumers (read the changed interface)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_models.py::TestAcceptanceCriterionModel` (line 765) \u2014 Extend with 4+ test cases: construction with trending_metric, construction without (backward compat), model_dump round-trip, validation error on invalid monotonic_direction.\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Other References\\n\\nNone identified.\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Producers (write the changed interface)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py::AcceptanceCriterion` \u2014 Add `TrendingMetricConfig` model (new Pydantic model); add `trending_metric: Optional[TrendingMetricConfig] = None` field to `AcceptanceCriterion` following the AliasChoices pattern (`validation_alias=AliasChoices('trending-metric', 'trending_metric')`, `serialization_alias='trending-metric'`). Also: add optional `metric_history` to `BookendVerification` OR create new `TrendingMetricResult` model (planner decision).\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/t0-baseline-capture.md` \u2014 Add branch in Step 2 per-criterion loop: when `trending_metric` present on criterion, also run `trending_metric.command` via Bash and record integer stdout as `metric_value`.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/tn-verification-gate.md` \u2014 Add branch in Step 2 per-criterion loop: when `trending_metric` present, run `trending_metric.command`, compare integer to T0 `metric_value`, assert `target_met` (current == target) and `monotonic_direction` (correct directional change from T0). Set `verdict: FAIL` if either fails.\\n\\n### Configuration / CI\\n\\nNone identified. Schema addition is additive and backward-compatible \u2014 no CI reconfiguration needed.\\n\\n### Design Intent Alignment\\n\\nAlignment assessment: ALIGNED\\n\\nThe `trending_metric` field is additive and optional \u2014 it extends `AcceptanceCriterion` without changing the contract for criteria that omit it. This aligns with the bookend system's design principle: T0 and TN iterate over the `acceptance_criteria_structured` list and act on each criterion independently. Adding a branch per criterion (\\\"does this criterion have a `trending_metric`? if so, also capture/compare the integer\\\") does not change the control flow for criteria without it.\\n\\nThe `BookendVerification` model at `models.py:421-449` currently carries `stdout_diff_summary` for text diff content. Implementation must decide whether to add `metric_history` as an optional field on `BookendVerification`, or create a separate `TrendingMetricResult` model. Either approach preserves backward compat for criteria without `trending_metric` \u2014 the field would default to `None`. The item does not prescribe the choice; the planner should evaluate model size and serialization impact.\\n\\nThe item correctly identifies that `AcceptanceCriterion` uses `AliasChoices` throughout (verified by fact-checker). The `trending_metric` new field must follow the same alias pattern (`validation_alias=AliasChoices('trending-metric', 'trending_metric')`, `serialization_alias='trending-metric'`) for consistency \u2014 this is already noted in the item's Effort section.\\n\\n**Note**: The item's Measurable Signal section uses `StructuredAcceptanceCriterion` \u2014 this class does not exist. The correct class name is `AcceptanceCriterion` (verified at models.py:365). The ACs are correctly written using `AcceptanceCriterion`. The Measurable Signal section example command should be corrected before implementation begins.\\n\\n### Documentation (will become stale)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` \u2014 Add `trending_metric` sub-fields (`command`, `target`, `monotonic_direction`) under the `acceptance-criteria-structured` section. Without update, documentation does not reflect the new optional field and plan authors cannot discover the capability.\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n\\n- [ ] Every code producer updated or verified compatible\\n- [ ] Every code consumer migrated to new interface\\n- [ ] Every stale document updated\\n- [ ] Every agent instruction updated\\n- [ ] Old interface deprecated or removed (if replacing) \u2014 N/A, this is purely additive\\n- [ ] CI/config files updated and validated \u2014 N/A, no changes required\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n**Type**: missing-guardrail\\n**Rationale**: The absence of `trending_metric` in `AcceptanceCriterion` allows plan authors to silently encode AC-as-task-list when they intend AC-as-outcome. The TN verification gate cannot detect or reject malformed multi-file migration criteria \u2014 it simply evaluates exit codes, never detecting that a count-based metric was supposed to reach a target value. The system permits the bad outcome (incorrect AC structure) that a schema guard should have prevented.\\n**Analysis Method**: none (missing-guardrail classification requires no root-cause analysis)\\n**Scenario Target**: Plan with multi-file migration task needing count-to-zero AC -> `AcceptanceCriterion` supports `trending_metric` field; T0 captures integer; TN asserts target reached and monotonic direction satisfied.\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n\\n| System | Role | Connection |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `sam_schema/core/models.py::AcceptanceCriterion` | Schema producer | Defines the data contract for structured ACs; extended with new optional field |\\n| `sam_schema/core/models.py::BookendResult` | Schema producer | Records per-criterion T0 state; may need `metric_value` field addition |\\n| `sam_schema/core/models.py::BookendVerification` | Schema producer | Records per-criterion TN state; needs `metric_history` or `TrendingMetricResult` |\\n| `agents/t0-baseline-capture.md` | Consumer (reads ACs) + Producer (writes T0 artifact) | Must branch on `trending_metric` and capture integer count |\\n| `agents/tn-verification-gate.md` | Consumer (reads ACs + T0 artifact) + Producer (writes TN artifact) | Must branch on `trending_metric`, run command, compare to T0, assert target + monotonic |\\n| `tests_sam/test_models.py::TestAcceptanceCriterionModel` | Test consumer | Must cover new field with 4+ cases |\\n| `docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` | Documentation | Must add `trending_metric` sub-fields |\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe `Task` model at `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py` accepts a new optional field on `acceptance-criteria-structured` entries: `trending_metric` with sub-fields `command` (shell command producing a single integer), `target` (expected final value, default 0), and `monotonic_direction` (\\\"decreasing\\\" or \\\"increasing\\\").\\n\\nThe `tn-verification-gate` agent's verification logic reads `trending_metric` entries on the task and:\\n\\n1. Runs each `command`, captures the integer\\n2. Compares against the T0 baseline value for the same metric\\n3. Asserts current value matches `target` AND has moved monotonically in `monotonic_direction` from T0\\n\\nThe `t0-baseline-capture` agent records every `trending_metric.command` output as a baseline.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRun: `uv run python -c \\\"from sam_schema.core.models import StructuredAcceptanceCriterion; print('trending_metric' in StructuredAcceptanceCriterion.model_fields)\\\"` \u2014 outputs `True`.\\n\\nRun a test plan with a `trending_metric` AC: `tn-verification-gate` output JSON includes a `metric_history` field listing T0 value and Tn value, with `monotonic_violated: false` and `target_met: true` when the command output matches `target`.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` lines 277\u2013304 (Bookend Task Ordering) defines T0 (baseline) and TN (verification) tasks. T0 captures pre-implementation state via `t0-baseline-capture` agent, and TN runs `tn-verification-gate` to verify acceptance criteria. The verification model is binary (criterion met vs. not met) \u2014 there is no representation for a *count metric* that should monotonically trend toward a target value across the implementation.\\n\\nThe Composio codebase-migrate pattern uses `rg 'jest\\\\\\\\.(mock|fn|spyOn)' | wc -l` after each batch merge \u2014 the count must trend to 0. Multi-file migration tasks today have no native way to express \\\"this count should be 0 by completion\\\" as a single acceptance criterion measurable at every wave or every commit.\\n\\nSymptom: a multi-file rename plan with `acceptance-criteria-structured` cannot encode \\\"count of `from \\\"jest\\\"` imports must be 0\\\" as a single observable metric. Instead, the AC must enumerate each file individually (which makes it AC-as-task-list, not AC-as-outcome) or be verified manually after the final merge.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"04833ec640e61172733c6e4ade82d50a0905ec8ad682c4556b36aa445e40d5a7\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPtX3aw\"}"}